Description: Biometric wakeups: display off until the verification result
 A device can declare the kind of its wakeups in the udev property
 POWERDEVIL_WAKEUP_TYPE (timer, powermanagement, network, telephony or
 biometric). Such a device counts as wakeup source when its event count rose
 during the sleep cycle: the wakeup count only counts while user space uses
 /sys/power/wakeup_count, which systemd does not do, so the detection of the
 wakeup source never matched.
 .
 After a wakeup by a biometric sensor the display stays off and the device
 goes back to sleep after 5 s without user input. The VerifyStatus signal of
 fprintd answers the touch: a match turns the display on, a rejected finger
 (no match, or a scan to repeat) too unless the fingerprint configuration of
 the device (/etc/lisbon/fingerabdruck.conf, WECKEN=dunkel) keeps it off. This
 also applies while the system is awake with the display off.
 .
 A full wakeup (org.kde.Solid.PowerManagement.wakeup) now ends the wait for
 user input after any wakeup that left the display off and starts the usual
 display idle time; before, the device went back to sleep after the idle time
 even though the consumer had turned the display on, and the display then
 stayed on without idle timeout.
